:: Money Parody Intro
<<silently>><<clotheson>><<handheldon>><</silently>>
The moment you try to turn around, you see someone in black. Black hair. Black eyes.
A black suit. The only break in all that black is a white cat snuggled against his shoulder,
entirely unbothered by any of this. And he looks... very Asian?!
<br><br>
"Hello! I know this is absurd, but this is also important! Lemme explain—EEUHHH..."
<br><br>
Then he exhales through his nose like a man trying not to open a file called <i>final_final_really_final_fix_this_time.twee</i>.
<br><br>
"You know, I have many things to do. Too many. Like, really too many. I open one thing,
then I remember another thing, then another thing comes from nowhere, then suddenly my brain says,
hey, maybe make a new event too! Why? No idea. Just suffer, I guess."
<br><br>
The cat gives a tiny meow.
<br><br>
"B-But... uhh, yeah, right. I should make it simple," he says to the cat. "But look at this!"
He points at you, or more precisely, <span class="red">at the absurd amount of money you somehow possess</span>.
"This is not normal rich. This is stupid rich. This is the kind of rich that makes the whole economy lie down and cry.
Maybe I should tax you."
<br><br>
A pause.
<br><br>
"No. Too normal. Maybe make a masked accountant instead."
<br><br>
He thinks about it.
<br><br>
"No, no, too much work. Need sprite. Need dialogue. Need reason. Need follow-up.
Then someone asks if the accountant can be romanced? Absolutely not. Maybe. No. Stop—"
<br><br>
And he's off. He paces back and forth, talking faster and faster, more to himself than to you. The cat yawns.
Somewhere in the middle, the words stop being words at all. His speech slides into something tonal and utterly foreign.
He doesn't appear to notice. He's still going.
<br><br>
<i>...what is his problem?</i>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Money Parody Take]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Money Parody Take
"Bleeehh," the man says abruptly. The white cat finally deigns to look at you.
<br><br>
"Anyway." He smiles, pleasant as anything, and snaps his fingers. "Gotta take your money!"
<br><br>
The floor drops out from under you. Your vision flares white, then folds into black. You don't even feel yourself hit the ground.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Money Parody Take 2]]>><<run setup.inflation.takeAllMoney()>><</link>>
<br>

:: Money Parody Take 2
<<set _moneyParodyReturn to $moneyParodyReturnPassage>>
<<if !_moneyParodyReturn or !Story.has(_moneyParodyReturn) or setup.inflation.PARODY_PASSAGES.includes(_moneyParodyReturn)>>
	<<set _moneyParodyReturn to $passagePrev>>
<</if>>
<<if !_moneyParodyReturn or !Story.has(_moneyParodyReturn) or setup.inflation.PARODY_PASSAGES.includes(_moneyParodyReturn)>>
	<<set _moneyParodyReturn to "Bedroom">>
<</if>>
<<earnFeat "Meet the Dev">>
When you come to, you're sprawled exactly where that impossible interruption found you. Your head pounds. No man. No cat.
<br><br>
On reflex you check your accounts. <span class="red">Your savings are gone</span> with every last impossible penny of it,
leaving only <<printmoney `setup.inflation.PARODY_LEFTOVER`>> in your pocket.
<br><br>
<i>Damn, he really took all the money. What <b>is</b> his problem?!</i>
<br><br>
<i><<link "“At least I'm not taking everything!”" _moneyParodyReturn>><<unset $moneyParodyReturnPassage>><</link>></i>
<br>
